{"title":"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each of three doors is painted one colour: either black or white or gold. Each colour is equally likely to be chosen for each door. What is the probability that at least one colour is not used?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea8f67840b6e490d85534350eda4a482fd694ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac79 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac59 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{20}{27} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac29 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"380\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For at least one color to <i>not</i> be used, the same color must have been chosen all three times or one color was chosen once while another color was chosen twice.\n</p><p>There would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to pick the same color three times because there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> different colors.\n</p><p>Next, if one color was chosen once while another color was chosen twice, there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to pick the color that was chosen once and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to chose to pick the repeated color. There are also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to order these colors because there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to chose the spot where the color that was chosen once is. There would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/809f20f06abdd729b08c2f6bd41443b025d903c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 2 \\times = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" /> different ways to do this.\n</p><p>Thus, there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0d195ed03b93698040992e8a8322ee88111e578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 + 3 = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> ways to have at least one color <i>not</i> being used.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bddc37dcba2e1e491535b290f280c208f7bcc02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{3} = 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> ways to color the doors because there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> different colors, so the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b011dbe8184ed5d1980fc9a39986bf24de0038b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{21}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, which would then simplify to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f1575c75456ac4fee4e827eb75454994d263a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } \\frac79}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"62\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For less than one color to <i>not</i> be used, black, white, and gold must have each been used for one door. Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db3b59940e4f5cd42bbab2b7815c452a0197507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3! = 6$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> ways to arrange these, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/f/8af6d758c0b907cd4a5087ecdea11310ac4ef297.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n! = n \\times (n - 1) \\times (n - 2) \\times \\cdots \\times 2 \\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"316\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bddc37dcba2e1e491535b290f280c208f7bcc02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{3} = 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> ways to color the doors, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d7aa2162fee33dc741b4dfe467386c18cbb178.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27 - 6 = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> of these would have had at least one color <i>not</i> being used.\n</p><p>The probability is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b011dbe8184ed5d1980fc9a39986bf24de0038b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{21}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f1575c75456ac4fee4e827eb75454994d263a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } \\frac79}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"62\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can denote black as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, white as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, and gold as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. We can then list the possibilities:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/1/021dba1da04c3f1738fe7f57075582fd77466441.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BBB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f04e1d4cf108624a70db23d7f49003f41cc7666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BBG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/e/2ae386236a44da28ce3a5133ce8e0a53e10fc6f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BBW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a183b75ce165ed1d3bef7af393f5c2bfe5ee9c17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BWB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a5d093563cac8d9facca3e891371880bb3cad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BGB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/625f3d16da894bf7802c571c59d5c566d2ffd43f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BWW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/9/1c9193eaae3fa31c21a8c639f05e871a3250edba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BWG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/e/ebedb2abf29287e0ae319de22bc1e8eb52ea2229.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BGW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fb2c00fee66d5607bd1dad1d770c05461e27651.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BGG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/3/653fb688f4188c971385ee104c07f75e91ce0fbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WBB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/f/4df4171f7639437c09cc1edea28b515ec6f82fe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WBW$\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/6/466890643f95fdd97063180809a35f558198b763.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WBG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f65bbf3cdae5f66320ec764917598ac8a2b0ab55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WWB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a072b279139c2ffd7bad79ba2e4980dcd9dd1855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WWW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441e6beab975aee4578c01f35f3df9440b5fa164.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WWG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c000593a2abcf938077a909dc47137ebe1dccb1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WGB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7ff600e88abef67dc6a872ffb443e7429302143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WGW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/645129fc9114ddbc364acce7b7b23152feb02913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WGG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a7c4957784ea84cad6ac31858955da771efdeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GBB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4a5ebe42cd5bd587a1c57c6ee62f235b0eb4734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GBW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96b06146601622e07f11eae28ecbc71cb648fdcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GBG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71c5b46c8f5ac0966ffd66bb80048cf11c2953a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GWB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b1ec3d31147d11e94188be4f73542a839603b56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GWW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f816aafb7f186350f06d4760b68297659cb8c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GWG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c7b1a3983c61222971a780c36a30b32bb541c29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GGB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/1/4c16cc0c8b105e42ea7d3d1e9f48bebd71bb6162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GGW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/f/59fc17c514809f5ae050d5d5598388b22de4d68c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GGG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Counting, we see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ways to color the doors, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> where there is at least one color <i>not</i> being used. We could have also realized that there was some mirroring because we could just swap out colors for other ones.\n</p><p>The probability is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b011dbe8184ed5d1980fc9a39986bf24de0038b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{21}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f1575c75456ac4fee4e827eb75454994d263a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } \\frac79}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"62\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Pro